# Stable Audio 3 — Latent Probing

This project extracts **Stable Audio 3 medium** VAE latents over four
music/audio datasets and probes whether the latents encode interpretable
musical information (instrument, dynamics, rhythm, pitch, structure).

The focus is **representation probing**, not generation.

🤗 **Hugging Face mirror (private):**
[`StoneYeY/sa-latent-probe`](https://huggingface.co/StoneYeY/sa-latent-probe)

```bash
# Teammate access (after invite):
git clone https://huggingface.co/StoneYeY/sa-latent-probe
# or
python -c "from huggingface_hub import snapshot_download; \
  snapshot_download('StoneYeY/sa-latent-probe', repo_type='model')"
```

## Results — all 4 datasets

7,090 clips: MAESTRO 2,000 (v3.0.0, 30 s windows) · Slakh 2,000 (30 s windows)
· Groove 1,090 (full files) · FSD50K eval 2,000 (full files). SA3-medium VAE,
bfloat16, chunked encoder.

### Probe A — instrument / style classification

| Dataset | Vocab (top-N) | Linear acc / f1 | MLP acc / f1 | Chance |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| FSD50K | 10 sound tags | 0.37 / 0.33 | **0.41 / 0.38** | 0.17 |
| Groove | 10 drum styles | 0.50 / 0.38 | **0.65 / 0.53** | 0.41 |
| Slakh | 10 instrument classes (rarest-non-universal heuristic) | 0.22 / 0.17 | **0.23 / 0.21** | 0.16 |

Slakh's modest accuracy reflects the difficulty of the task (almost every
track contains Bass / Drums / Guitar / Piano; we predict the rarest non-universal
class), not a model failure.

### Probe B — loudness regression (R²)

| Dataset | RMS linear → MLP | LUFS linear → MLP |
